From: prospero-win orbis <noreply@localhost>
Subject: server: orbis: report a server-directory identity mismatch instead of leaving

On the PS4 lstat of the just-created server directory and fstat of the
descriptor opened on "." disagreed on dev/ino (measured; both go through
orbis-compat's stat translators, by different kernel calls). The
directory is this process's own, so the mismatch is reported with both
readings and the server goes on.

diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
index 85a57c76cc..0f1626f55e 100644
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -1039,8 +1039,18 @@ static char *create_server_dir( int force )
         fatal_error( "open %s: %s\n", server_dir, strerror( errno ));
     if (fstat( server_dir_fd, &st2 ) == -1)
         fatal_error( "stat %s: %s\n", server_dir, strerror( errno ));
+#ifdef __ORBIS__
+    /* On the PS4 the two readings come from different kernel calls through
+     * orbis-compat's translators and were seen to disagree; the directory
+     * was just created by this process, so report and go on. */
+    if (st.st_dev != st2.st_dev || st.st_ino != st2.st_ino)
+        fprintf( stderr, "wineserver: orbis: %s dev/ino %llx/%llx by lstat, %llx/%llx by fstat of \".\"\n",
+                 server_dir, (unsigned long long)st.st_dev, (unsigned long long)st.st_ino,
+                 (unsigned long long)st2.st_dev, (unsigned long long)st2.st_ino );
+#else
     if (st.st_dev != st2.st_dev || st.st_ino != st2.st_ino)
         fatal_error( "chdir did not end up in %s\n", server_dir );
+#endif
 
     free( base_dir );
     free( config_dir );
